    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n81545" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περικλύζω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>wash all round</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ παιδίον ὕδατι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Mir.</u>
					837b21
				</span></i>
			:— 
				Pass.
			, <i>to be washed all round</i> by the sea, of an
			island, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				6.3
			</span></i> ; of a boat, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Mar.</u>
				36
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μὴ περικλύζοιο θαλάσσῃ</span>,
			i.e. venture not on the sea, <i><span class="en">
				Arat.
				287
			</span></i>: metaph., <i>to be overwhelmed</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κακοῖς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lib.
					<u>Decl.</u>
					30.61
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῷ πλήθει τῶν σκοπῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Gal.
					15.584
				</span></i>
			.</div>
